summary:
I reviewed U3b on GREEN run-2's exact bytes in sc-s74-ct (HEAD 4c0f3c99), from 19:20:15 to 19:47, and changed nothing in the worktree. The 23 files hash identically at the first and last check, and the RED set is intact (the new files match their red/ copies and the 11 test files show +90/-363). The diff passes every engineering check I ran:
- The fence sha re-derived with the node one-liner equals 372c5048...1a02.
- The catalogs are 1004/1004; only aiConsent.body changed and the 3 profile.aiSharing keys are gone.
- CRLF and LF are intact per file, there is no .snap, no credential shape, and gitleaks finds nothing.
- Full jest: 366 suites and 3559 tests passed, 42 snapshots.
- tsc rc 0; eslint 0 errors.
- The backend set is 315 passed (T23 green), plus 103 related backend files whose only failures are pre-existing (the baseline list, and test_prompt_truth's tiktoken errors, which also fail at base).
- Repo greps find no code caller of get_client with an argument and no os use left in openai_service.py.

Of my 18 byte-copy mutants under the lock, 16 were killed by named nodes:
- the version left at 1;
- v1 records still counting;
- the EN sentence after the final sentence;
- the AR sentence missing;
- a one-word EN change;
- a 5th toggle host;
- a stale t('profile.aiSharing.title');
- the master save still sending ai_sharing_enabled;
- the title inside the ScrollView;
- an absolute maxHeight;
- the ScrollView removed;
- the private arm with the env name written out;
- per-user routing under a new name;
- a renamed get_client parameter;
- the route rejecting the field;
- the route not storing the field.

Two survived. B17, the docstring still saying opt-out: add an OpenAPI B5 node. B12E, the private arm with the env name built by concatenation: add an api_key check to B3's kwargs.

There are no blocking findings. The one major finding is that the UB-R13 card cap (maxHeight 85%, with only the body able to shrink) plausibly pushes 'Not now' (AX3) and 'Agree and continue' (AX4) off-screen on a 667-pt iPhone SE at accessibility text sizes. Without the cap they stay on screen, and nothing in src caps font scaling. That is arithmetic, not a device run. The recommended fix is to cap the ScrollView with a number from useWindowDimensions, or to set maxFontSizeMultiplier on the fixed texts. A minor related point: at default size on the SE, the new OpenAI sentence starts around wrapped line 9-11 of a body window about 9 lines tall, with no scroll affordance; flashScrollIndicators fixes that. The other minors are stale comments. The notes record that the legal text still promises the toggle (UB-R4, process-only), that row 12's api.ts anchors were already wrong at HEAD, and that the coverage floor was not measured.
